        "original_id": "b850a04d-d787-57ca-a5e5-729027bd2c3f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Speedpass\n- Companies: Mobil Oil Corp., ExxonMobil, McDonald's, Verifone\n- Places: Chicago area, San Jose, California\n- Topics: Electronic payments, point-of-sale technology\n\nFacts:\n- In 1997, Mobil Oil Corp. introduced Speedpass, a keychain RFID device for electronic payment.\n- In 1999, Mobil Oil Corp. merged with Exxon to become ExxonMobil.\n- McDonald's deployed Speedpass in over 400 restaurants in the Chicago area.\n- Verifone is an American multinational corporation headquartered in San Jose, California.\n- Verifone provides technology for electronic payment transactions and value-added services at the point of sale.",
